        "fortimanager:index/wantempSystemVirtualwanlinkHealthcheckSla:WantempSystemVirtualwanlinkHealthcheckSla": {
            "description": "Service level agreement (SLA).\n\n\u003e This resource is a sub resource for variable `sla` of resource `{{% ref #/resources/fortimanager:index%2FwantempSystemVirtualwanlinkHealthcheck:WantempSystemVirtualwanlinkHealthcheck %}}`. Conflict and overwrite may occur if use both of them.\n\n## Import\n\nWantemp SystemVirtualWanLinkHealthCheckSla can be imported using any of these accepted formats:\nSet importOptions = [\"wanprof=YOUR_VALUE\", \"health_check=YOUR_VALUE\"] in the provider section.\n\n```sh\n$ export \"FORTIMANAGER_IMPORT_TABLE\"=\"true\"\n$ pulumi import fortimanager:index/wantempSystemVirtualwanlinkHealthcheckSla:WantempSystemVirtualwanlinkHealthcheckSla labelname {{fosid}}\n$ unset \"FORTIMANAGER_IMPORT_TABLE\"\n```\n\u003e **Hint:** The scopetype and adom for import will directly inherit the scopetype and adom configuration of the provider.\n\n",
            "properties": {
                "adom": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Adom. This value is valid only when the `{{% ref #/resources/fortimanager:index%2FwantempSystemVirtualwanlinkHealthcheckSla:WantempSystemVirtualwanlinkHealthcheckSla/properties/scopetype %}}` is `{{% ref #/resources/fortimanager:index%2FwantempSystemVirtualwanlinkHealthcheckSla:WantempSystemVirtualwanlinkHealthcheckSla/properties/adom %}}`, otherwise the value of adom in the provider will be inherited.\n"
                },
                "fosid": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "SLA ID.\n"
                },
                "healthCheck": {
                    "type": "string",
                    "description": "Health Check.\n"
                },
                "jitterThreshold": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Jitter for SLA to make decision in milliseconds. (0 - 10000000, default = 5).\n"
                },
                "latencyThreshold": {
                    "type": "number",
                    "description": "Latency for SLA to make decision in milliseconds. (0 - 10000000, default = 5).\n"
